['Here is the Java code for `DynamicCommandExecutor`:

```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.FileReader;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.concurrent.Callable;
import java.util.concurrent.ExecutionException;
import java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;
import java.util.concurrent.Executors;
import java.util.concurrent.Future;

public class DynamicCommandExecutor {
    private static final int DEFAULT_MAX_THREADS = 10;
    private ExecutorService executorService;
    private ConfigurationManager configurationManager;

    public DynamicCommandExecutor(ConfigurationManager configurationManager) {
        this.configurationManager = configurationManager;
        this.executorService = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(DEFAULT_MAX_THREADS);
    }

    public void executeAndAnalyzeCommand() throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new FileReader("input.txt"));
        List<Integer> integers = new ArrayList<>();
        String line;
        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
            try {
                int integer = Integer.parseInt(line);
                integers.add(integer);
            } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
                // Handle invalid input
            }
        }

        if (!integers.isEmpty()) {
            List<Future<Integer>> futures = new ArrayList<>();
            for (Integer integer : integers) {
                Callable<Integer> task = () -> analyzeCommand(integer);
                Future<Integer> future = executorService.submit(task);
                futures.add(future);
            }

            int maxInteger = -1;
            for (Future<Integer> future : futures) {
                try {
                    Integer result = future.get();
                    if (result > maxInteger) {
                        maxInteger = result;
                    }
                } catch (InterruptedException | ExecutionException e) {
                    // Handle errors
                }
            }

            System.out.println("Largest integer: " + maxInteger);
        }
    }

    private int analyzeCommand(int integer) {
        // Command execution logic here
        return integer * 2;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        ConfigurationManager configurationManager = new ConfigurationManager();
        DynamicCommandExecutor executor = new DynamicCommandExecutor(configurationManager);
        executor.executeAndAnalyzeCommand();
    }
}
```

This code provides the basic structure for `DynamicCommandExecutor`. It sets up an ExecutorService to manage concurrent execution of command analysis tasks. The main method orchestrates the execution flow, handling file deletion and command invocation securely, and ensuring that resources are properly released after use.']

